Currently: optional::transform never materializes against gcc-16
headers and main verifies vacuously (0 assertions).  Sibling of
cpp23_optional_monadic (which uses the host's headers).

ROUND-104 TRIAGE: the first error is `symbol '_M_payload' is unknown`
while instantiating _Optional_base<int, TRUE, TRUE>.  gcc-16's payload
is `_Storage<_Stored_type> _M_payload;` where _Storage is a NESTED
member UNION template with a defaulted bool NTTP
(`template<typename _Up, bool = is_trivially_destructible_v<_Up>>`)
and P0848 conditionally-trivial destructors (`~_Storage() = default;`
plus `constexpr ~_Storage() requires (!is_trivially_destructible_v<_Up>)`).
Four hand kernels all PASS (negative results, /tmp/k104/os1-os4):
plain constrained dual dtor; union with defaulted trait NTTP; the same
nested inside a class template; variable-template trait in the NTTP and
requires-clause.  Per the no-hand-guessing rule the carrier is being
cvise-reduced instead: /tmp/cv105, gate = pinned driver + tumbleweed
g++ 16.2 validity (docker image gcc16-gate, via `sg docker` -- root-owned
`sudo` children crash cvise's kill_pid_queue with psutil.AccessDenied)
+ CBMC `_M_payload' is unknown` + `could not fully type-check`.

ROUND-106: carrier replaced by the finished cvise artifact (fleet
/tmp/cv105): 7327 lines -> 50 lines.  VALIDITY NOTE: the artifact uses
gcc-16-only builtins (__add_rvalue_reference as a type-yielding
builtin, variable-template partial specializations of the _v traits),
so g++ 13 / clang 18 REJECT it -- validity is certified by g++ 16.2 in
the `gcc16-gate` docker image (tumbleweed), which accepts it with the
__CPROVER_assert declaration prefixed.  CBMC still reports the pinned
signature (`symbol '_M_payload' is unknown`).  Visible structure: the
_Optional_payload primary takes 3 trait-valued defaulted bool NTTPs,
has a 1-arg partial specialization and a 3-arg one, and _Optional_base
names `_Optional_payload<int>` with all defaults -- the choice among
partial specializations under defaulted, trait-valued NTTPs is the
suspect layer.

ROUND-106 ROOT CAUSE (backward-delta on the 50-line artifact): the
load-bearing element is `is_trivially_move_assignable_v<_Tp>` -- a
FUNCTION template whose parameter type is the gcc-16 type-yielding
builtin `__add_rvalue_reference(_Tp)` -- named inside _Optional_payload's
defaulted bool NTTP conjunction.  Instantiating that function template
reports `symbol '__add_rvalue_reference' is unknown` (see
gcc16_builtin_type_param_instantiate, 8 lines), so the NTTP default
cannot evaluate and the payload member never materializes.  A second
independent defect: the NAMED-parameter form of the same declaration
does not parse (gcc16_builtin_type_param_named).  Fixing the
instantiate defect should cascade here; re-check this test after.
